      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In this study brain tumors developing with tuberous sclerosis were biologically benign; total transcortical tumor removal permanently relieved the attending cerebral hypertension and achieved prolonged survival without notable functional impairment. In tuberous sclerosis, hamartomas characteristically develop from a random focal defect in organogenesis that affects many organ systems, sometimes seriously altering their function. Thus, genetic penetrance primarily determines the over-all prognosis, and \"hereditary multiple system hamartomatosis\" accurately describes the disease."},
